{
  "_comment": "Voxel hair for scripts/entity/HairBuilder.gd, DMZ's strand model (com.dragonminez.common.hair, recovered with javap) scaled up to read as Dragon Ball silhouettes. Coordinates are head-local model units: the head cube spans x[-4,4] y[0,8] z[-4,4], y=0 is the head pivot (neck), y=8 the top of the skull, z=-4 the face and z=+4 the back of the head; 16 units = 1 block. A style has `groups` (DMZ's 68 slots: FRONT 1 row x 4 cols, BACK/LEFT/RIGHT/TOP 4x4, col offsets [-3,-1,1,3], row drop [0,-1.5,-3,-4.5], base rotations FRONT -90x BACK +90x LEFT +90z RIGHT -90z TOP none) for caps and manes, and `strands` for hand placed spikes (`at` position, `rot` euler, `mirror` also emits the X mirrored twin). `point` narrows a strand along its length so a spike ends in a point; a strand at +x fans OUT with a positive rot.z and converges with a negative one. `accent: true` puts a strand on a second surface with its own colour (two tone hair). Transformation hair is derived, not authored: see `form_hair` and HairBuilder.FORM_DERIVE.",
